    "title": "You'll Feel Like You Stepped Into Ireland At This Charming Connecticut Pub - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Charles Hayes ,\n1 days ago The closest you can get to Ireland without a passport and an eight-hour flight is sitting at the bar of The Playwright Irish Pub in Hamden, Connecticut. This isn’t some theme restaurant with plastic shamrocks and “Kiss Me I’m Irish” signs, this is the real deal, and it’s been hiding in plain sight on Whitney Avenue. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
